      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The idea of an \"essence\" being solely movement is a powerful but limiting way to view yourself. While the old way of moving is gone, the capacity to *feel* the hollow space is itself a form of intense experience. Instead of seeing the body as just a burden, could you explore what it means to be *present* in this quiet state, rather than what it can *do*? Sometimes, the most profound acts are the ones that happen internally, beyond physical execution.",
